# Safety-net timer for the DomainSifter archive page generator — fires at
# 14:00 UTC daily.
#
# WHAT IT RUNS
# domainsifter-archive.service, i.e. scripts/archive_generator.py: reads
# src/data/daily-domains.json, generates one Markdown reference page per
# new Clean/Promising domain via Anthropic Haiku, appends to
# src/data/archive-index.json, then commits and pushes to origin/main.
#
# THIS IS A SECOND TRIGGER, NOT THE ONLY ONE. Read this before assuming
# the archive was unscheduled: domainsifter.service (and
# domainsifter-force.service) already chain it with
# `OnSuccess=domainsifter-archive.service` in their [Unit] section. That
# is the PRIMARY trigger and it is working. `systemctl list-unit-files`
# reporting domainsifter-archive.service as `static` is the CORRECT state
# for a unit with no [Install] section that another unit starts — it is
# not evidence that nothing fires it. See RECOVERY.md "Archive didn't run"
# and the 2026-05-21 STATE.md entry for commit 623b947.
#
# WHY A TIMER ON TOP OF OnSuccess=
# OnSuccess= fires only when the pipeline unit exits 0. On a day the
# pipeline fails — CZDS outage, RDAP ban, push rejection — the archive
# never runs at all, even though yesterday's still-unarchived
# Clean/Promising entries are sitting in daily-domains.json waiting.
# _filter_qualifying has no date filter, so an independent daily fire
# drains that backlog without operator intervention. On a normal day this
# timer is a cheap no-op: the chained run already archived everything, the
# index dedupes, the generator logs "No new qualifying domains", and
# nothing is committed or pushed.
#
# WHY 14:00 UTC
# The pipeline starts at 09:00 UTC (domainsifter.timer) and currently
# finishes between 11:45 and 12:25 UTC — the upper end after the LLM
# ranker came back on 2026-09-19 and added ~25 min. The chained archive
# run then takes roughly another 20 min of Haiku calls before ITS own
# commit and push. So the realistic worst case today is the pipeline's
# push at ~12:25 and the chained archive's push at ~12:45.
#
# 14:00 UTC buys ~95 minutes past the worst observed pipeline finish and
# ~75 minutes past the chained archive's finish. That margin is deliberate
# and is about pushes, not CPU: run-daily.sh and archive_generator BOTH
# `git push` to origin/main, and a push landing while origin has moved is
# exactly how this project broke on 2026-05-21 (see RECOVERY.md,
# "Pipeline succeeded, push failed"). The gap must absorb a slow run, not
# merely an average one. It also leaves 19 hours of clearance before the
# next 09:00 UTC pipeline start, so a long archive backlog drain cannot
# run into tomorrow's window either.
#
# Note that systemd will not run two instances of the same unit
# concurrently: if this timer somehow fires while the OnSuccess-chained
# run is still active, the start job queues behind it rather than racing
# it. The 14:00 choice is about the PUSH window, which systemd cannot
# serialize for us because the pipeline's push comes from a different
# unit.
#
# Persistent=true matches domainsifter.timer: a missed 14:00 UTC firing
# (server down) runs on next boot instead of waiting a day. This is safe
# for the archive — it is idempotent and the same-day guard deliberately
# does not apply to it (RECOVERY.md). One caveat for the operator: a boot
# catch-up can fire at an arbitrary time, including mid-pipeline. If it
# does, the archive reads a daily-domains.json from the previous run and
# may push while the pipeline is still working toward its own push. That
# is a recoverable push rejection, not data loss, and the recipe is the
# "Pipeline succeeded, push failed" scenario in RECOVERY.md.
#
# INSTALL (server-side, run as root once):
#   cp /home/domainsifter/domainsifter/systemd/domainsifter-archive.timer /etc/systemd/system/
#   systemctl daemon-reload
#   systemctl enable --now domainsifter-archive.timer
#   systemctl list-timers | grep domainsifter   # confirm next 14:00 UTC firing
#
# Logs: journalctl -u domainsifter-archive.service -f

[Unit]
Description=Run DomainSifter archive page generator at 14:00 UTC

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 14:00:00 UTC
Persistent=true
Unit=domainsifter-archive.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
